WEBVTT

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:23.640
OK, people,
Eastern Seaboard coming online.

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:25.800
We got scarers coming out.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:30.520
(DRAMATIC BRASS
FANFARE PLAYING)

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:38.080
(BELL DINGS)

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.640
They are so awesome.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.000
(GROWLING)

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:14.640
(SNARLS)

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:32.040
Hey, may the best monster win.

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:33.520
I plan to.

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:34.760
(BELL RINGING)

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:38.560
We are on in seven, six, five,

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:42.400
four, three, two...

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:46.960
(SNARLS)

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:50.840
You're the boss.
You're the big hairy boss.

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:56.640
(CHILD SCREAMING)

00:01:58.480 --> 00:01:59.480
(BELL DINGS)

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:01.840
I'm feeling good today, Mikey.

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:04.240
(BEEPING)

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:06.880
Attaboy. Another door coming right up.

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:11.000
(CHILD SCREAMING)

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:14.840
(GROWLING)

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:16.120
You're still behind, Randall.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:19.320
-Maybe I should realign the scream...
-Get me a door.

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:20.400
Door, yes, door.

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:21.840
(CHILD SCREAMING)

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:29.000
(BEEPING)

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:34.480
(CHILDREN SCREAMING)

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:36.800
(BELLS DINGING)

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.680
Well, Jerry, what's the damage so far?

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:51.920
We may actually
make our quota today, sir.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:53.880
First time in a month.

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:56.520
(GURGLING AND BURPING)

00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:57.600
(GASPING)

00:02:57.680 --> 00:02:58.720
(DOOR BUZZING)

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:01.320
(SCREAMING AND SOBBING)

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:03.520
-What happened?
-The kid almost touched me.

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:06.720
-She got this close to me.
-She wasn't scared of you?

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:09.280
-She was only six.
-I could have been dead.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:13.040
-I could have died.
-Keep it together, man.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:14.120
(WHISTLING)

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.000
Hey, we got a dead door over here.

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:19.120
-I'm coming.
-Look out.

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:21.040
Excuse us.

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:26.480
We've lost 58 doors this week, sir.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.640
Kids these days.

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:30.920
They just don't get scared
like they used to.

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:33.000
Let her rip.

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:34.320
(BUZZING)

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:41.240
(EERIE BLUBBERING)

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:44.040
(CHILD SCREAMING)

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:46.480
-Sir?
-What?

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:48.320
Look.

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:52.600
CELIA ON PA: Attention.
We have a new scare leader.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:54.320
Randall Boggs.

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:55.840
(ASSISTANTS CHEERING)

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:57.400
Look at those numbers.

00:03:57.480 --> 00:03:58.960
(CHILDREN SCREAMING)

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:02.880
(KNUCKLES CRACKING)

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:04.480
Slumber party.

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:05.520
Whoo!

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:07.120
(BEEPING)

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:08.840
CELIA ON PA: Never mind.

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:10.800
Hey, watch it.

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:13.360
(LAUGHING)

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:16.640
Well, James,
that was an impressive display.

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:19.040
Just doing my job, Mr. Waternoose.

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:20.560
'Course I did learn from the best.

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:21.720
(BOTH LAUGHING)

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:25.080
If I don't see a new door
in my station in five seconds,

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:27.400
I will personally
put you through the shredder.

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:28.560
(SCREAMS)

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:33.360
Hey, Wazowski, nice job.
Those numbers are pretty sweet.

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:36.000
Are they?
You know, I hadn't even noticed.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:38.760
-And how's Georgie doing?
-He's doing great.

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:40.880
I love working with that big guy.

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:43.400
Keep the doors coming.
I'm on a roll today.

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:47.240
George and I are like brothers. 2319!

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:48.880
We have a 2319!

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:50.320
(GASPS)

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:53.240
(ALARM BLARING)

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:55.120
COMPUTER VOICE: Red alert.

00:04:56.920 --> 00:04:58.160
Red alert, red alert.

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:00.360
-Red alert.
-FEMALE ON PA: George Sanderson.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:04.400
Please remain motionless.
Prepare for decontamination.

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:06.080
JERRY: Duck and cover, people!

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:11.800
WATERNOOSE: Not the CDA.

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:15.920
(SIREN WAILING)

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:20.440
CDA AGENT 1: Go, go, go.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:22.040
CDA AGENT 2: Coming through.
Stand aside.

00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:23.760
Clear the contaminated area.

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:26.240
CDA AGENT 1: A 2319 in progress.

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:28.400
CDA AGENT 2: Coming through.
Watch yourself.

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:29.600
(GROANS)

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:31.080
(WHIMPERING)

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:35.840
CDA AGENT 1: Stand back. Careful.

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:43.960
(ALL GASPING)

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:45.920
(MUFFLED EXPLOSION)

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:54.000
CDA AGENT 1: All clear. Situation is
niner-niner-zero. Ready for decon.

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:57.480
-Thanks, guys, that was a close one.
-CDA AGENT 1: OK.

00:05:57.840 --> 00:05:59.280
(GEORGE SCREAMING)

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:03.720
(WHIMPERS)

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:07.840
(SCREAMING)

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:12.880
JERRY: Take a break. We gotta
shut down and reset the system.

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:15.480
An entire scare floor out of commission.

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:17.560
What else can go wrong?

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:23.160
-What a day.
-We're just going through a rough time.

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:25.440
Everyone knows
you'll get us through it.

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:28.040
Tell that to the board of directors.

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:33.680
James, this company's been
in my family for three generations.

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:36.720
I would do anything
to keep it from going under.

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:38.040
So would I, sir.

00:06:40.640 --> 00:06:43.560
-I could use your help with something.
-Anything, sir.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:48.040
We've hired some new scare recruits,
and frankly, they're...

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:51.200
-Inexperienced?
-They stink.

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:54.120
I thought maybe
you might come by tomorrow

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:56.240
and give them a demonstration.

00:06:56.360 --> 00:06:59.280
Show them what it takes
to be our top scarer.

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:02.520
I'll start out with the old
Waternoose jump and growl.

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:04.040
(GROWLING LOUDLY)

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:08.840
Now that's my boy.

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:12.960
(RINGING)

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:17.560
JERRY: Let's go, everybody.
All doors must be returned.

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:19.200
No exceptions.

